  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Haitian and Salvadoran soldiers have taken control of the Stade Sylvio Cator in Port-au-Prince, ending two years of gang control.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-12:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "On 11 November, Fils-Aimé stated that the Salvadoran intervention was helping the Haitian government regain control of territory.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385920278:70"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "El Salvador has intervened militarily in Haiti since 21 October 2026, after a gang ambush on 18 October kidnapped four Salvadoran Gang Suppression Force (GSF) aviation technicians.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385920278:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The stadium is Stade Sylvio Cator in Haiti, where the reports place the takeover.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-12:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "On 6 November, a 400 Mawozo spokesperson told the Associated Press (AP) that the gang was ready to enter peace negotiations and undergo disarmament in exchange for an end of \"international interference\" in Haiti.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:week:1385920278:74"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:00:40Z",
      "text": "On 8 November, Salvadoran helicopters and a Task Force loitering munition struck a house belonging to Joseph, described as 400 Mawozo's alleged headquarters, killing up to 20 gang members.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:week:1385920278:68"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:00:47Z",
      "text": "Before 10 November, US chargé d'affaires to Haiti David Howell stated that three Salvadoran soldiers had been injured and one had been medically evacuated back to El Salvador.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:week:1385920278:78"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:00:56Z",
      "text": "The article lists two sides: on one, the Gang Suppression Force and Task Force mercenaries with logistical support; on the other, Haitian gangs including 400 Mawozo and Chèn Méchan.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1385920278:side-1",
        "wiki:box:1385920278:side-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:01:03Z",
      "text": "Wikipedia lists the conflict's status as ongoing.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1385920278:status"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:01:10Z",
      "text": "As Wikipedia records them from its sources, casualties are 3 Salvadorans injured on one side, a figure El Salvador denies, and about 32 killed on the other.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1385920278:casualties-side-1-",
        "wiki:box:1385920278:casualties-side-2-"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:01:19Z",
      "text": "The takeover is reported by France 24.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-12:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-12T00:01:27Z",
      "text": "The sources are Wikipedia, Current events, Wikipedia articles, Wikimedia pageviews and Wikidata, and each caption links to the evidence it rests on.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-12:1",
